  <h2>What is BIRD2WORD?</h2>
  <p>BIRD2WORD is a word ladder game. You're given a start word and a target word, both four letters long. Your job is to turn one into the other by changing exactly one letter at a time — and every step along the way has to be a real word.</p>

  <h2>A quick example</h2>
  <p>To go from BIRD to WORD, one path looks like this:</p>
  <div class="example">
    <div class="step">
      <div class="tile">B</div><div class="tile">I</div><div class="tile">R</div><div class="tile">D</div>
    </div>
    <span class="arrow">&rarr;</span>
    <div class="step">
      <div class="tile">B</div><div class="tile">A</div><div class="tile">R</div><div class="tile">D</div>
    </div>
    <span class="arrow">&rarr;</span>
    <div class="step">
      <div class="tile">W</div><div class="tile">A</div><div class="tile">R</div><div class="tile">D</div>
    </div>
    <span class="arrow">&rarr;</span>
    <div class="step">
      <div class="tile">W</div><div class="tile">O</div><div class="tile">R</div><div class="tile">D</div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p>Each word differs from the one before it by a single letter. That's the whole game — simple to learn, but the shortest path isn't always obvious.</p>

  <h2>How to play</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Type your guess.</b> On desktop, just type on your keyboard. On a phone, tap the puzzle board and your keyboard will pop up.</li>
    <li><b>Press Enter</b> to submit a word. If it's a real word and only one letter away from your last word, it gets added to your chain.</li>
    <li><b>Tile colors</b> give you feedback: blue means that letter matches the target word, yellow means that's the letter you just changed.</li>
    <li><b>Backing up</b> is easy — just retype a word you already used (or the start word) and your chain rewinds to that point, no penalty.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Modes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Random by Difficulty</b> — Easy, Medium, or Hard puzzles, pulled at random from a dictionary of nearly 5,000 four-letter words.</li>
    <li><b>Fun Word Pairs</b> — a curated set of especially fun or clever start/target pairs.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Flip It</h2>
  <p>Stuck, or just want a change of pace? Hit <b>Flip It</b> at any time to swap your start and target words. Nothing you've already solved is lost — the words you've used simply reappear on the board from the other end, already filled in. You just need to build a path until you connect to them. Flip as many times as you like.</p>

  <h2>Mercy</h2>
  <p>If you want to give up on a puzzle, hit <b>Mercy!</b> and confirm. The rest of the path will be filled in for you so you can see how it plays out. Give-ups don't count toward your stats or score — they're just there so you're never stuck.</p>

  <h2>Scoring</h2>
  <p>Your score rewards solving a puzzle in as few words as possible, and rewards speed too — though word-efficiency matters more than time. Harder puzzles (ones with a longer shortest path) score higher. After you solve a puzzle, you can also tap "Shortest possible" in the results to reveal one example of the most efficient path.</p>

  <h2>Stats</h2>
  <p>Your average and best time, word count, and score are tracked separately for each mode and difficulty, right in your browser. They stay on your device and aren't shared anywhere.</p>

